"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-04-12T21:45:06Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T17:25:04Z","closed_at":"2026-04-14T16:34:16Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.6.2.stable.mono.official [71f334935]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - AMD Ryzen 9 3900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 63.91 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nDistraction Free Mode (Ctrl+Shift+F11) is not distraction free. It only hides the left and right panel but does not hide the bottom panel. The whole point of Distraction Free mode is to fullscreen the viewport without fullscreening the entire app (hiding the OS taskbar). Current implementation fails to do that.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Have any tab of the bottom panel open, for example Output or Shader editor\n2. Enable Distraction Free Mode by clicking the button or pressing the shortcut (Ctrl+Shift+F11) \n\nResult: Distraction Free Mode temporarily hides only side panels, not bottom panel\nExpected: The Distraction Free mode is Distraction Free. It maximizes the viewport while hiding all other panels.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n-","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com